      en: ["Founded in 1730 as a major silver mining center.", "Coordinates: 13.9333° N, 86.8500° W.", "Designated as a National Monument of Honduras in 1979.", "Home to the most famous aguardiente distillery in the country.", "Located in the foothills of the Montserrat Biological Reserve.", "The town features over 30 abandoned historic mine entrances.", "Serves as the political capital of the El Paraíso department.", "Known for its cool climate and steep, colonial-style streets."],
