      en: ["Formerly known as 'Las Piedras' until the mid-19th century.", "The city's elevation is approximately 680 meters (2,231 ft).", "Key economic driver is the processing and export of Arabica coffee.", "Located at coordinates 14.33°N and 87.68°W.", "Features a historic district with Spanish colonial architecture.", "Home to the Roberto Suazo Córdova Stadium.", "Served by the CA-7 highway, a major regional artery.", "Part of the Comayagua Valley economic development zone."],
